      "scenario": "Any applied training, consumed nonempty stats array, or positive level award calls EncodeAutomaticRoot, which uses Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes. Actual SaveBaseStats, SaveStatPointsRootAsync and ProcessStatsIncreasedAsync publish through FileSystemManager.WriteFileAtomicAsync, whose encoder adds EF BB BF. Thus every changed image differs from its owner encoding although parsed values can match.",
      "requirement": "P2 fixed owner serializer and exact three after-images; exact calculation prerequisite for the pre-seal automaticPlan.",
      "evidence": [
        "BookOfEternityClient/Services/CharacteristicsService.cs:275",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Services/CharacteristicsService.cs:381",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/GameEngine/GameEngine.TurnLifecycle.cs:2493",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/FileSystemManager.cs:764",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/FileSystemManager.cs:4322",
        "BookOfEternityClient.Tests/MortalJointAutomaticCalculationTests.cs:170"
      ],
      "requested_correction": "Use the existing pure owner byte encoder for changed images, preserve exact untouched images, and add independent raw-byte assertions for the real owner control plus all three changed images. The test JSON reader must decode the permitted preamble.",
      "validation_status": "Confirmed by pinned source comparison; reviewer executed no reproducer. Existing 33-case GREEN misses the mismatch because the control compares parsed stat values."
    },
    {
      "id": "T179PA-F02",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "title": "Case-insensitive JsonNode access accepts lone noncanonical field aliases",
      "location": "BookOfEternityClient/Services/CharacteristicsService.MortalJointAutomatic.cs:94",
      "scenario": "PropertyNameCaseInsensitive=true is passed through JsonNode deserialization into JsonObject node options. A lone experience field Level is read as level; lone UnspentStatPoints/LevelUpStatPointsAwardedThroughLevel supply initializer evidence; lone StatsIncreased is processed and consumed. StrictJsonAuthority rejects duplicate case pairs, but a single alias has no duplicate and is accepted.",
      "requirement": "Strict canonical field/alias policy and unchanged actual owner source selection. The ordinary owners use exact field spellings; malformed sources must refuse rather than acquire canonical meaning.",
      "evidence": [
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/StrictJsonAuthority.cs:14",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Services/CharacteristicsService.cs:283",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/GameEngine/GameEngine.TurnLifecycle.cs:2432",
        "BookOfEternityClient/Core/GameEngine/GameEngine.TurnLifecycle.cs:2516"
      ],
      "requested_correction": "Keep duplicate and case-collision detection while parsing/reading canonical fields case-sensitively; explicitly reject lone case aliases of consumed fields so they cannot silently fall back or be ignored. Add negative examples covering the independent optional and required roots.",
      "validation_status": "Confirmed by candidate and dependency source, with .NET 8 primary-source confirmation of option propagation; reviewer executed no reproducer."
